----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var p = (1, "a")

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let n = p.0 + 1

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

set p.1 = "b"

----------
expect all three units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `p` = (1, "b") |
| 2 | reads `p` (1) | compiles, runs | new | `n` = 2 |
| 3 | updates `p` (1) | compiles, runs | new | - |

----------
scriptunit-edit 2
----------

let n = p.0 + 2

----------
expect unit 2 is edited
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | unit 2 reads only `p.0`, which unit 3 does not write | `p` = (1, "b") |
| 2 | reads `p` (1) | recompiles, runs | edited | `n` = 3 |
| 3 | updates `p` (1) | untouched | nothing it uses changed | - |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | reruns | tracks bindings by name, so the write to `p.1` counts as a write to all of `p` |
| 3 | reruns | writes `p` again after unit 1 reruns |
